{
  "lesson": 35,
  "title": "Makharij & Sifat",
  "titleArabic": "المخارج والصفات",
  "kind": "letters",
  "audioPath": "audio/lesson35/",
  "perPage": 6,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "p13",
      "title": "Hams (whisper)",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Hams = whisper. With كۡ let a little air flow out, like a soft whisper."
    },
    {
      "id": "p14",
      "title": "Hams (whisper)",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Hams = whisper. With تۡ let a little air flow out, like a soft whisper.\nSay تۡ softly with a little air — it is not a qalqala letter, so no bounce."
    },
    {
      "id": "p15",
      "title": "Tafkheem review",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Heavy letters خ ص ض غ ط ق ظ: full, deep sound. With a kasra, خ غ ق get a little lighter.\nKasra makes only خ غ ق less heavy. Fatha or damma keeps them fully heavy."
    },
    {
      "id": "p16",
      "title": "Tafkheem review",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "These never get lighter: ص ض ط ظ. Even صِ ضِ طِ ظِ stay fully heavy.\nSame deep sound in all three boxes."
    },
    {
      "id": "p17",
      "title": "The Lam in ٱللَّه",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "The ل of ٱللَّه is heavy after fatha or damma (or when you start), light after kasra. Every other ل is light.\nلِلَّهِ is a short spelling: لِ + ٱللَّه. The ٱ and one ل are not written."
    },
    {
      "id": "p18",
      "title": "Raa",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Heavy ر: full, deep sound. Light ر: thin sound. Read the rule above each table first.\nHeavy (1): ر has a fatha:  رَ\nHeavy (2): رۡ comes right after a fatha\nHeavy (3): Stopping: رۡ comes after a sakin letter (not ي), and before that a fatha"
    },
    {
      "id": "p19",
      "title": "Raa",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Heavy (4): ر has a damma:  رُ\nHeavy (5): رۡ comes right after a damma\nHeavy (6): Stopping: رۡ comes after a sakin letter, and before that a damma"
    },
    {
      "id": "p20",
      "title": "Raa",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Start ٱرۡ with إِ. This kasra is borrowed, so رۡ stays heavy.\nHeavy (7): رۡ after a kasra, then a heavy letter (without kasra) in the same word\nHeavy (8): رۡ after a kasra that is not original (borrowed)"
    },
    {
      "id": "p21",
      "title": "Raa",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "Light (1): ر has a kasra:  رِ\nLight (2): رۡ after an original kasra, with no heavy letter after it"
    },
    {
      "id": "p22",
      "title": "Raa",
      "titleArabic": "",
      "hint": "فِرۡقٍ: heavy or light when you keep reading; heavy when you stop on it.\nمِصۡرَ and ٱلۡقِطۡرِ: heavy or light only when you stop. Preferred: مِصۡرَ heavy, ٱلۡقِطۡرِ light.\nLight (3): Stopping: رۡ comes after a sakin letter that is not heavy, and before that a kasra\nLight (4): Stopping: رۡ comes after a yaa leen  ـَيۡ"
    }
  ],
